  "body": "Opened by the branch-disposition execution (2026-11-07) from branch `queue/9855-5950-clippy-test-modules`.\n\nBranch origin: queue branch for issue #9855.\nThis branch was laptop-local work (or a stranded remote branch) with real changes ahead of `main` and no PR. Per Drew's 2026-11-07 branch-disposition ruling, ahead branches with real changes get a PR; this PR surfaces the work for triage instead of leaving it stranded on a branch.\n\nTriage owner: batch issue in developing-today/code, \"Unowned PR batch from branch disposition (2026-11-07)\". Outcome per batch triage: close with reason, or route to impl/finish/merge as a follow-on fix task.\n\nEvidence: branch-ahead review `~/workspace/scratch/branch-ahead-review-2026-11-07.md`; execution log `~/workspace/scratch/branch-disposition-2026-11-07.md`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796704680&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7199&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7199&signature=a63c616e85fac3debf352f4d8671d99c68e5b40e8f361fa06748de294490e1d2\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7199?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n---\n\nShepherded by task 13131 (repo-health queue). This PR scopes the pkgs/id clippy unwrap/expect/panic exceptions to test modules per the issue #5950 policy: test-module allows only, no crate-wide or package-wide allows, and production-code diagnostics fixed in code (including the fallible ledger API adaptation and its design record, which also dispositioned the Codex P1 finding — fix commit b079b45f48).\n\nFixes #5612\nFixes #5950\n",
